00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:27.200
And he's been knocked up early in the morning
by these bloody French already.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:31.720
We're going to deal with them well after one,
he hasn’t got the papers with him or anything.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.680
Does he not have the authority to accept it?

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.760
No, he absolutely has
the authority to accept it.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:36.680
He just didn't want to?

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:41.520
Yes, why might he have done that, why might he
have turned away a conditional surrender,

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:43.960
and insisted that no,
it's got to be unconditional?

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:47.040
Saw an easy career promotion
with a crushing victory.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.160
Oh, crushing victory is interesting.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.160
-I was going to say...
-Crushing loss, I don't know.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:55.880
A sly glance. An impropriety at
a society party. I don't f***ing know.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:12:00.640
No, he... he was saying we can get
a crushing victory, essentially, to them.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.040
Was he getting a bonus if he won?

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:08.200
No, he was bluffing, he was flat out bluffing
that he had more people and more on the way,

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:12.320
and, 'If you don't surrender you will all die,
there are no conditions on this.'

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:17.040
"You can't come into the pub because it's
full of men, full of them you hear, full of them.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.920
"Well, no you can't, you simply can't
come through the door.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.720
"I can't accept your surrender,
there's far too many of us, bye.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:22.800
"Well, lads."

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:24.520
And so there is some speculation here,

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:28.440
that he got a little bit of help from some people
looking on from the cliffs.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.720
So what did the French see on the cliffs?

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.000
People?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.920
Turn of the 18th century,

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.960
does anyone know what
a traditional Welsh costume looks like for women?

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:43.960
Yes, the pointy hat and the little apron
and they tie it under your thing,

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.920
and then, yeah, yeah, like that,
you look like a little Welshwoman,

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.600
on all the spoons that they sell
at the seaside resorts.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:52.120
They sell spoons, alright,
they have Welsh ladies on them.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:56.080
I'll give you the point,
it's a top hat and a red dress.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:56.880
Yeah.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.240
Now, if you're looking at someone far away
on the top of a cliff…

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:01.360
Oh s***, he didn't think he'd seen
more soldiers, did he?

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.400
Yes.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.880
Because they had a shako
and the red coat,

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:12.520
so he's confused a bunch of watching Welshwomen
for a force of infantry, is what you're saying?

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:15.800
That is the speculation,
that he looked up at the top of the cliffs,

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.920
and thought, 'There's a lot of people up there,

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.280
'and they look like soldiers.'

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:24.480
One, invent glasses, two, whatever happens
in your life, whatever it is,

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.360
you're never going to be the man

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:30.320
who confused a load of Welshwomen
in traditional dress for backup.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.320
So what do the French do?

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.280
Run away.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:36.720
Unconditional surrender, yes,
I'll give you the point.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:40.160
The French surrender, the British accept it,

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:42.040
Tate is imprisoned briefly,

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.600
and then returns to France
along with most of the force.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:48.720
There is something about this invasion though,

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:51.880
there is something; 1797, this was.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:56.080
And there's something special about it,
something that is marked out every time,

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:59.880
on every little…
on every little memorial plaque about this,

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:03.880
there is something about the invasion
of mainland Britain in 1797.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.880
That will be the last invasion
of mainland Britain.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.440
Mystery Biscuits.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:15.400
Unlike - going back to the start of this,
so it's not thrown together - 1066,

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.120
which is what everyone else thinks it is.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.680
Yes, you are absolutely right.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:27.680
The Battle of Fishguard was the most recent
landing on mainland Britain

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:29.760
by a hostile foreign force.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:30.760
As we record this...

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:34.800
-And on that note...
-Wow.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.920
congratulations,
Gary, you win the show.

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:46.400
You have won a device to help cool the lower
jaws of South American rodents.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.600
It's a chinchilla chin chiller.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.200
So with that we say thank you to Chris Joel.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.560
Thank you.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.680
To Gary Brannan,

00:14:58.560 --> 00:14:59.560
to Matt Gray.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:02.120
I've been Tom Scott,
and we'll see you next time.

